# Cohestra: cost-aware Cursor + BMAD delivery

This is an efficiency rule, not a shortcut around the mandatory review loop in `AGENTS.md` and `_bmad/custom/mandatory-code-review-loop.md`. All existing authorization, tenant isolation, security, test, owner release, and exact-HEAD requirements still apply.

## Route each separate agent run
- **Grok 4.7 High, Fast OFF (standard)**: architecture, high-risk privacy/security design, release decisions, and final independent BMAD/CAT-SEC review.
- **Composer 2.5, Fast OFF (standard)**: bounded implementation, bug fixes, unit/integration regression tests, and focused refactoring.
- One Cursor run uses its selected model. Do not pretend to change models during a run. At task handoff, state the recommended model/settings; the owner or agent launcher must select them explicitly. If standard speed is unavailable, disclose the actual mode.
- Avoid paid third-party models unless specifically authorized. Keep on-demand usage disabled unless owner explicitly changes that preference.

## Work efficiently, with evidence
1. Start with a one-paragraph objective, current SHA, changed files, mandatory acceptance criteria, and smallest relevant test set. Prefer a fresh, scoped run to a huge accumulated conversation.
2. Inspect the actual diff and affected callers/data flows first. Expand to the whole repository only for a demonstrated cross-cutting risk. Do not repeatedly re-read unchanged files or duplicate independent investigations.
3. TDD: reproduce each verified defect with a failing test, implement the smallest safe fix, then run targeted tests. Existing GitHub Actions runs are the source of truth for full exact-SHA CI; never substitute unverified local claims.
4. Preserve mandatory BMAD code review and required independent review layers. Focus each layer on distinct risks and the changed HEAD. After **any** code change, rerun applicable tests/review on the new HEAD; passing old-SHA evidence is stale.
5. Launch additional subagents only for necessary, distinct, parallelizable scopes. Avoid multiple agents editing the same files, speculative feature additions, repeated review passes without new evidence, and broad documentation churn.
6. Compact handoffs: objective | exact SHA | tests/checks with links | verified BLOCKER/MAJOR and reproduction | next action. Summarize logs; do not paste full logs or files unless needed to investigate.
7. Stop when the applicable code-review/product-acceptance gates pass or there is a proven blocking dependency. Missing, skipped, canceled, timed-out, neutral-required, or failed mandatory checks are **not** PASS.

## Current beta boundaries
- Cohestra invite-only beta only; attendance check-in and live billing are out of scope.
- Keep release candidate PR #561 DRAFT until separately owner-approved. Do not merge, deploy, change UAT variables/secrets, or touch live data as a side effect of this rule.
- Production remains NO-GO. Autonomous-delivery development remains paused.
